<propeller version="1.1" name="X1 lift fan, upper">
  <!-- Blades designed for the X1 concept model, not the manufacturer's fan: 13 twisted NACA 4409 blades, chord 50-66 mm, pitch 42-24 deg root to tip, r 0.175-0.5475 m in a 44 in duct -->
  <!-- design point: hover at race weight in a rear duct, upper tip Mach 0.5, loading rising as sqrt(r), lift coefficient 0.9 root to 0.7 tip; the lower fan straightens the upper's swirl at 0.72 of its speed -->
  <!-- solid CFRP blades 1600 kg/m3 0.246 + aluminium hub ring 2700 kg/m3 0.102 kg m2; the motor rotor is not included -->
  <ixx unit="KG*M2"> 0.3473 </ixx>
  <diameter unit="M"> 1.0950 </diameter>
  <numblades> 13 </numblades>
  <!-- Blade element + momentum per annulus: both fans of the duct share one axial velocity, the lower one runs in the upper one's swirl, -->
  <!-- lower/upper speed 0.72 (torque balance); no tip loss (10 mm gap); wake area ratio 0.72 = the concept model's 1.13 duct gain; three 35 mm stator struts as drag, CD 2.5 (NACA TN 3038); -->
  <!-- NACA 4409 polars: thin-airfoil zero-lift angle, Abbott & von Doenhoff slope, stall and standard-roughness drag trends, element Reynolds number, Korn/Lock drag rise; tables at this fan's tip Mach 0.50; -->
